scenario the sky empties at once, and the boundary that decides when that counts
describe From an open sky to nothing between two epochs. Physically that is a
describe lid closing over the antenna; it is also what a transmitter capturing
describe the receiver looks like from the outside. Neither is a normal reading.
describe
describe There are two separate detectors behind ConstellationAnomaly and this
describe fixture exists to keep them apart, because until it did they were not.
describe The earlier version of this trace asserted the blackout with `sats 9 0`
describe — nine satellites used out of none in view — which is the *impossible
describe reading* detector, a different branch that fires first. Deleting the
describe blackout branch entirely left this scenario green. A trace that passes
describe for a reason unrelated to its name is worse than no trace, because it
describe is counted.
describe
describe So each step below is arranged so that exactly one branch can explain
describe it, and the mutation that removes that branch fails this file.

at 0
  fix 3d
  pos 5000000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  sats 10 12
  hdop 90
  jam none
  spoof none
  expect validity valid
  expect trust trusted
  expect no-reason constellation-anomaly

# The blackout, on its own. Nought used out of nought in view: `used > in_view`
# is false, so the impossible-reading branch cannot be what raises this. Twelve
# satellites one second ago and none now is the only thing left.
at 1000
  fix 3d
  pos 5000000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  sats 0 0
  hdop 90
  jam none
  spoof none
  expect reason constellation-anomaly

# The sky comes back, poor but real. The anomaly is retracted rather than left
# to age out — evidence is cleared the moment the condition stops holding.
at 2000
  fix 3d
  pos 5000000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  sats 5 7
  hdop 180
  jam none
  spoof none
  expect no-reason constellation-anomaly

# The boundary, and the reason there is one. Seven satellites is not an open
# sky, so seven going to nought is a bad sky getting worse — an ordinary thing
# under a bridge or a roof — and calling it an anomaly would fire this detector
# on half of everyday indoor use. The threshold is `previous >= 8`; this pins
# the side of it that must stay quiet.
at 3000
  fix 3d
  pos 5000000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  sats 0 0
  hdop 180
  jam none
  spoof none
  expect no-reason constellation-anomaly

# And the other detector on its own. Six in view, so the blackout branch cannot
# fire; nine of them used, which no receiver can do. This is the impossible
# reading, and it is the strongest form of the check available without
# per-signal carrier-to-noise data.
at 4000
  fix 3d
  pos 5000000 10000000
  alt 42000
  acc 3500
  sats 9 6
  hdop 120
  jam none
  spoof none
  expect reason constellation-anomaly
